# commit-msg-hash-resolves.baseline
#
# Grandfathered dangling commit-message hash citations: hashes that exist
# as git objects but are NOT reachable from HEAD (orphaned cherry-pick
# objects whose content landed under a rewritten hash).  Listed here so
# the reachability gate does not block on pre-existing citations while
# still failing on any NEW unreachable citation.  One 12-hex token per
# line; '#' comments allowed.  These entries are permanent — origin/master
# is not advancing in this fork (origin/master == a9da9240ca1a).  Do not
# add to this file to silence a new citation -- fix the citing message
# instead.
#
# Each dangling hash has a reachable twin at the same subject; the twin is
# recorded in the comment above its entry.  The citing messages carry
# in-message annotations (stale X -> Y form or X ("subject") form).
#
# twin: a79d41c36e2b ("stats/json: fix missing comma before ip6mr_churn in network section")
331e499fdb5c
# twin: e8f741787a65 ("childops/af-unix-scm-rights-gc: re-check getppid after PDEATHSIG")
53a4b05beea8
# twin: fa70568f8e3e ("stats: latch ferror and disable timeseries sink on write failure")
726c4417688b
# twin: 119cd4932b3c ("check: fix window-section threshold miss to SKIP instead of FAIL")
84b8dd492f47
# twin: 6eb5db2242fd ("scripts: add hash-subject resolver and citation convention")
e13204eec1a7
# twin: b526ecb0c675 ("io_submit: gate post_state deref with looks_like_corrupted_ptr")
f9a2e3f2cc06
